          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP301 Leduc

The rec centre was busy today but the area around the cap was beyond the bustle.  Some flagging in a tree guided us to the deep hole containing the cap.  Thanks for another cap, ofth!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684093122">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP301 Leduc

Out getting a few more BCPs south of Edmonton. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Princess really wanted to visit the dog park near the cap. Since did get to meet some of the puppies from a Saturday morning dog group. The cap itself was easy to find in its hole. Needed to do a bit of cleaning to read the numbers. Otherwise in good shape. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for all the BCPs and the fun I've had over the last couple weeks getting most of the ones in the Edmonton area. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
